# This file IS committed — it holds defaults and placeholders only.
# Put real connection strings, API keys, and secrets in `.env.local`, which
# `.gitignore` ignores and which overrides every value here. See DATABASE.md,
# "Where Credentials Go".

# The PostgreSQL database the app reads and writes. REQUIRED — there is no
# default, and app/lib/prisma.ts throws without it rather than quietly opening
# some other database. Read by the app and by the Prisma CLI (db push, studio).
#
# Copy this line into `.env.local` with your real values. Any PostgreSQL works:
# a local install, a container, or a hosted project.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/thinking_map
#
# Deploying? Use the POOLED string (port 6543) for the app and the DIRECT one
# (5432) for `prisma db push`. See DATABASE.md, "Deploying".

# OPTIONAL, and normally left unset. The integration tests start their own
# PostgreSQL and stop it afterwards, so `npm test` needs nothing here. Set this
# only to run them against a database you already have — and use a DIRECT
# connection, since `db push` needs a real session.
#
# Must stay COMMENTED OUT when unused: an empty `TEST_DATABASE_URL=` would
# still be a set-but-blank value to some readers, and point the suite at
# nothing instead of at the database it would have started for itself.
#
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/postgres
